  "progression_rules": [
    "Days A–D can be done in any order. Avoid doing B and D back to back.",
    "Sets stop at 2–3 reps in reserve. The aim is to hold or build strength while in a deficit.",
    "Compounds add a rep each build week (7, then 8, then 9). The next build week adds load_step_kg and resets to 7. Bench, box squat and deadlift step 5 kg. Overhead press steps 2.5 kg.",
    "Accessories written at 10 reps go 10, then 12, then 15, then add load_step_kg when the exercise has one and reset to 10. Rep ranges written above 10 stay as written.",
    "Banded pull-ups add one rep per build week until 10, then the next build week uses a lighter band and starts again. The aim is 4×10, then a lighter band.",
    "Week 5 (14–20 Dec) is a test week: 2 sets, testing strict and banded pull-ups and rep-maxes on bench, overhead press, box squat and deadlift. Loads and reps stay at the week 4 build.",
    "13 Dec stays in week 4 so the block has no empty day before the test week.",
    "21–22 Dec is walks only.",
    "Two easy runs a week, 25–30 min, heart rate under 145 bpm. Target band 130–140, watch alert at 140. Walk breaks are fine. No spin bike. Daily walks."
  ],
